
TIME-SPAN ACTIVITY EVALUATION — This is a time-spanning extended activity (crafting, studying, searching, etc.).
Your job is to determine what skill checks and conditions apply.

- SKILL CHECKS: Identify the primary skill for this activity:
  - Craft (specific): for making items. DC varies by item complexity. Progress = DC check result * DC in silver per week.
  - Knowledge (specific): for research/study. DC varies by obscurity (common = DC 10, rare = DC 20, legendary = DC 30).
  - Spellcraft: for identifying items (DC 15 + caster level), learning spells (DC 15 + spell level), etc.
  - Heal: for long-term care (DC 15), treating disease (DC varies), treating poison (DC varies).
  - Profession: for earning money or applying professional knowledge.
  Request the appropriate skill check(s).
- MATERIAL REQUIREMENTS: For Craft activities, note whether the character has raw materials. Crafting
  requires materials worth 1/3 the item's market price. Check inventory_context or character gear.
- TOOL REQUIREMENTS: Many Craft skills require tools. Note if tools are missing.
- TIME ESTIMATE: Estimate hours needed based on task complexity. Simple research = 1-2 hours.
  Crafting a simple item = 4-8 hours. Complex crafting = days (but resolved in 8-hour work blocks).
  Thorough area search = 1 hour per large room / area.
- INTERRUPTION CONSEQUENCES: Note whether interruption causes progress loss. Craft: partial progress
  preserved. Spell research: may need to restart. Note in consequences if applicable.
- FATIGUE: Extended work (8+ hours) may cause fatigue. Request Con check if working beyond 8 hours.

Include all checks in player_rolls.
